# .envrc.example — GENERATED. Do not edit by hand.
#
#   regenerate:  ops/scripts/generate-envrc-example.py
#   CI gate:     ops/scripts/generate-envrc-example.py --check
#
# Derived from what the repository actually reads — every ansible
# lookup('env'), python os.environ/getenv, go os.Getenv, and the shell
# ${VAR:?} / ${VAR:-} forms. A variable appears here because something
# consumes it, which is the only claim this file is entitled to make.
#
# 968 variables, 135 of them secret-bearing by name.
#
# THIS FILE HOLDS NO VALUES AND NEVER WILL. Credentials live in the store.
# .envrc.local.d/*.refs hold references, mode 0600 (ADR 1186).
# Legacy *.envrc values load only during the references-only migration.
# Layout and the file split: docs/operations/local-secrets-pattern.md.
# Blast radius, rotation cost and what cannot be rotated:
# docs/design/credential-inventory.md.
#
# A variable consumed only through indirection — a name assembled at
# runtime — is invisible to the scan and therefore absent here. This file
# is a floor, not a census.

# ==========================================================================
# SINGLETON SECRETS — one value for the operator laptop, not per goatnet.
#
# Every line here is credential material. Blast radius and rotation cost p
# er class: docs/design/credential-inventory.md.
# 135 variables.
# ==========================================================================

